        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-24T15:31:45+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-24T15:31:45+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-24T06:01:45Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-24T06:01:45Z">
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system and associated trough continue moving over southern SA tonight and will move into the eastern states by late Tuesday. A high pressure system will move in from the west to be over SA on Wednesday. Another trough approaches the southwest during Thursday evening, and may linger about the western parts of SA before another high moves across the south over the weekend.</text>
                <text type="preamble">Wind and wave forecasts are averages. Wind gusts can be 40 per cent stronger than the forecast, and stronger still in squalls and thunderstorms. Maximum waves can be twice the forecast height.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
